1
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:16,917
This is now a antibacterial
satellite or a chemical in the world.

2
00:00:18,826 --> 00:00:23,337
ten, ten, ten, ten, ten,

3
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:32,780
Thank you.

4
00:01:28,280 --> 00:01:30,200
Let's go.

5
00:02:28,540 --> 00:02:31,340
Let's go.

6
00:03:01,460 --> 00:03:04,580
I don't know.

7
00:03:48,760 --> 00:03:49,819
Satsang with Mooji

8
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:02,110
Wait a minute.

9
00:04:03,180 --> 00:04:04,480
Who are you guys?

10
00:04:04,940 --> 00:04:06,760
Stay away from me. Damn it.

11
00:04:21,980 --> 00:04:23,340
Oh, for Pete's sake.

12
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:24,835
What a mess that was.

13
00:04:25,340 --> 00:04:29,222
Surrounded by that lot, I wondered
what was going to happen to us.

14
00:04:29,860 --> 00:04:33,507
Back there, it sounded like many
of them were saying Bakshish.

15
00:04:33,780 --> 00:04:35,604
What do you suppose that means?

16
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:38,040
It means, give me money.

17
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:41,340
I should have known that.

18
00:04:41,640 --> 00:04:45,120
What a backward little
hellhole this place is. My God!

19
00:04:47,020 --> 00:04:47,850
Polnareff,

20
00:04:47,940 --> 00:04:52,157
once you get used to it, you'll understand
the good things about this country.

21
00:04:52,240 --> 00:04:54,557
I'd never get used to a place like this.

22
00:04:54,640 --> 00:05:00,140
But this chai, or whatever you called
it, this is actually fairly decent stuff.

23
00:05:01,020 --> 00:05:03,297
I think it's a pretty interesting country.

24
00:05:03,380 --> 00:05:04,920
I really kind of like it.

25
00:05:05,460 --> 00:05:07,360
Jotaro, do you really mean that?

26
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:10,071
How can you say that with a straight face?

27
00:05:10,900 --> 00:05:13,900
They say once you live in
a place, it grows on you.

28
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:18,780
I don't get it.

29
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:23,802
You Asian guys must lack any sense of beauty
or elegance to like a place like this.

30
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:24,750
Whatever.

31
00:05:26,020 --> 00:05:27,680
I'm gonna go take a shit.

32
00:05:31,020 --> 00:05:32,680
What a vulgar man!

33
00:05:33,620 --> 00:05:34,450
Oh.

34
00:05:34,900 --> 00:05:36,540
Our dishes have arrived.

35
00:05:37,420 --> 00:05:38,250
Ah.

36
00:05:38,333 --> 00:05:39,840
And they look delicious.

37
00:05:46,860 --> 00:05:47,690
Ah.

38
00:05:47,773 --> 00:05:49,777
Just as I would expect
from a tourist cafe.

39
00:05:49,860 --> 00:05:51,300
A clean bathroom.

40
00:05:52,680 --> 00:05:53,510
Hmm.

41
00:06:03,260 --> 00:06:05,860
India getting close.

42
00:06:08,900 --> 00:06:09,730
Huh?

43
00:06:13,700 --> 00:06:14,530
Huh?

44
00:06:19,040 --> 00:06:19,900
You are...

45
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:26,750
What?!

46
00:06:26,833 --> 00:06:27,663
No one there.

47
00:06:27,746 --> 00:06:28,597
Did I imagine it?

48
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:32,209
I'm sure I saw some strange guy
outside the window just now.

49
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:49,870
What?

50
00:06:49,953 --> 00:06:50,783
No way!

51
00:06:54,660 --> 00:06:55,490
What?

52
00:06:55,573 --> 00:06:56,403
What is he?

53
00:06:56,520 --> 00:06:58,696
Why can I only see him in the mirror?

54
00:07:01,140 --> 00:07:02,200
That guy!

55
00:07:02,540 --> 00:07:03,640
A right hand!

56
00:07:05,660 --> 00:07:06,720
Not good!

57
00:07:08,540 --> 00:07:10,000
Oh no you don't!

58
00:07:10,200 --> 00:07:11,520
Silver Chariot!

59
00:07:21,140 --> 00:07:22,280
Goddamn shit!

60
00:07:22,780 --> 00:07:23,900
Where is he?

61
00:07:25,220 --> 00:07:26,920
Where did he disappear to?

62
00:07:36,580 --> 00:07:39,051
Now, where is the main body of that stand?

63
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:45,880
God damn it!

64
00:07:46,060 --> 00:07:48,942
I'll never find him in a
crowded place like this!

65
00:07:52,200 --> 00:07:53,820
What happened, Polnareff?

66
00:07:55,400 --> 00:07:57,880
At last, I found him. It's him.

67
00:07:58,520 --> 00:08:00,700
The bastard who killed my sister.

68
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:02,580
I finally found him.

69
00:08:03,800 --> 00:08:06,120
Now, just hold on, Polnareff.

70
00:08:06,340 --> 00:08:08,820
I understand how you feel, but calm down.

71
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:10,600
It could be an enemy trap.

72
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:13,437
Wait, you say?

73
00:08:13,520 --> 00:08:16,117
You say you understand my feelings?

74
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:19,220
I must say you impress me, Avdol. What?

75
00:08:19,820 --> 00:08:23,740
My younger sister and I, we lost
our parents at an early age.

76
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:27,400
We tried our best to get by
all on our own after that.

77
00:08:28,260 --> 00:08:31,300
Then my sister was brutally
violated and murdered!

78
00:08:32,020 --> 00:08:34,117
These feelings of mine...

79
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:37,297
You'd have to live through
that to ever understand them!

80
00:08:37,380 --> 00:08:38,660
That's the only way!

81
00:09:07,180 --> 00:09:08,200
Mr. Joestar,

82
00:09:08,560 --> 00:09:13,442
I'm sorry, but it's time I part ways with
all of you and continue my journey alone.

83
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:17,520
What do you mean by that, Polnareff? Hmm?

84
00:09:19,140 --> 00:09:22,669
Now that I know my sister's
assailant is somewhere close by,

85
00:09:22,880 --> 00:09:25,400
I can't rest easy until I find him.

86
00:09:28,260 --> 00:09:32,260
Even though you don't know his face
or the true nature of his stand?

87
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:37,140
I know both of his hands are right
hands, and that's good enough for me.

88
00:09:37,620 --> 00:09:40,540
They say the tomb robber
becomes the mummy.

89
00:09:41,100 --> 00:09:42,571
What do you mean by that?

90
00:09:43,320 --> 00:09:44,580
Now just a minute.

91
00:09:45,020 --> 00:09:48,680
You think that this guy
is going to defeat me?

92
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:50,717
I'm saying it's dangerous.

93
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:53,388
You'd be all alone
against an unknown stand.

94
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:57,360
So, Avdol,

95
00:09:57,860 --> 00:10:00,457
I heard that when you met
Dio for the first time,

96
00:10:00,540 --> 00:10:02,952
you were so frightened that you ran away.

97
00:10:03,080 --> 00:10:04,315
What is that you say?

98
00:10:06,640 --> 00:10:08,699
I've been alone from the beginning.

99
00:10:09,300 --> 00:10:12,620
I have fought all of my
battles alone, until now.

100
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:16,150
Listen up!

101
00:10:16,300 --> 00:10:18,124
I'll make this perfectly clear.

102
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:21,656
First of all, I don't care
about that guy Dio one bit.

103
00:10:22,340 --> 00:10:27,037
I believe I told you that I was only coming
along with you to seek my own vengeance.

104
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:30,000
Paul Naref, don't try to stop him, Avdol.

105
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:32,760
Yes, but Mr. Joestar...

106
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:35,220
It's all right. Let him go.

107
00:10:36,620 --> 00:10:37,980
As expected, Mr.

108
00:10:38,080 --> 00:10:40,300
Joestar, you're very understanding.

109
00:10:42,240 --> 00:10:43,580
Well, see ya.

110
00:11:00,280 --> 00:11:04,880
Well, looks like we'd gone and provoked
that boy, didn't we, Mr. J. Kyle?

111
00:11:19,960 --> 00:11:20,790
It's you.

112
00:11:22,960 --> 00:11:26,277
What happened to you
yesterday I waited such a long

113
00:11:26,360 --> 00:11:30,077
time hold your horses did
I promise I'd be there

114
00:11:30,160 --> 00:11:33,857
no oh no please I want
to stay with you for the

115
00:11:33,940 --> 00:11:37,577
rest of my life stop talking
crazy like hell you just

116
00:11:37,660 --> 00:11:41,717
barely turned 16 girl I'm
old enough to marry and

117
00:11:41,800 --> 00:11:45,517
I love you with all my
heart hey I'm just a drifter

118
00:11:45,600 --> 00:11:49,197
I got no home I live this
whole life day to day

119
00:11:49,280 --> 00:11:52,162
and in the end I'm destined
to die on the street.

120
00:11:54,380 --> 00:11:55,300
Listen to me.

121
00:11:57,260 --> 00:11:59,997
You come from one of them
aristocratic families.

122
00:12:00,080 --> 00:12:03,117
You shouldn't be thinking about
marrying old cowboy like me,

123
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:06,671
even though we love each other
so very, very much, you see.

124
00:12:07,580 --> 00:12:08,640
Is that true?

125
00:12:08,960 --> 00:12:12,917
Can you say that you love me more
than anyone else in the whole world?

126
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:13,830
You bet.

127
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:16,688
More than anyone else
in a whole wide world.

128
00:12:18,640 --> 00:12:19,800
So you see.

129
00:12:21,060 --> 00:12:24,560
It's because I love you
so much I can't marry you.

130
00:12:25,020 --> 00:12:26,580
You understand, don't you?

131
00:12:26,980 --> 00:12:30,260
Oh, darn, this is so
heartbreakingly difficult for me.

132
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:31,460
Oh, yes?

133
00:12:31,840 --> 00:12:34,640
I'll hold you like this from time to time.

134
00:12:34,880 --> 00:12:36,409
That's good enough for me.

135
00:12:37,440 --> 00:12:38,270
All right.

136
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:44,100
Well, you best run on home.

137
00:12:44,220 --> 00:12:45,737
Your parents be worried about you.

138
00:12:45,820 --> 00:12:47,291
Yes, I'd better be going.

139
00:12:55,160 --> 00:12:57,260
Well, that was damn annoying.

140
00:12:59,720 --> 00:13:03,249
You're probably thinking I'm
just complicating things again.

141
00:13:03,520 --> 00:13:08,108
But it's mighty damn convenient to have
that kind of woman all over the world.

142
00:13:08,260 --> 00:13:09,907
They'll do anything for you.

143
00:13:10,040 --> 00:13:12,260
Even sacrifice their lives.

144
00:13:13,660 --> 00:13:18,360
You already know the way I like to
do things, don't you, Mr. J. Guile?

145
00:13:19,560 --> 00:13:23,720
Well, just as we expected,
Polnarev's gone off by his self.

146
00:13:23,980 --> 00:13:26,317
Reckon we ought to go
kill him now or what?

147
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:27,230
Yeah.

148
00:14:08,140 --> 00:14:08,970
Hey there.

149
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:10,358
Listen up, partner.

150
00:14:10,940 --> 00:14:13,737
Somebody asks you if you've seen a
man whose hands are both right hands.

151
00:14:13,820 --> 00:14:16,408
Send him over towards
the outskirts of town.

152
00:14:17,540 --> 00:14:19,880
Yes, yes, of course, Kainzor.

153
00:14:25,020 --> 00:14:26,960
Step one completed.

154
00:14:41,620 --> 00:14:44,257
Have you seen a man whose
hands are both right hands?

155
00:14:44,340 --> 00:14:45,520
Eh, I don't know.

156
00:14:45,760 --> 00:14:46,640
Thanks a lot.

157
00:15:17,020 --> 00:15:19,380
Everything is ready, partner.

158
00:15:21,780 --> 00:15:26,280
Now we just wait for the
prey to step into our trap.

159
00:15:45,520 --> 00:15:48,340
Oh, my God.

160
00:16:14,340 --> 00:16:15,170
Well, now.

161
00:16:21,260 --> 00:16:22,680
Shall we hit the trail?

162
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:27,920
You know, with your stand, the hanged
man and mind the emperor being partners,

163
00:16:28,240 --> 00:16:29,880
we can kill them all.

164
00:16:54,420 --> 00:16:56,714
I was able to find some transportation.

165
00:16:57,160 --> 00:16:59,219
We can leave whenever you're ready.

166
00:16:59,660 --> 00:17:00,490
Right.

167
00:17:00,573 --> 00:17:01,414
Shall we get underway?

168
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:08,160
Avdol-san, what's...

169
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:23,160
What's wrong, then?

170
00:17:25,540 --> 00:17:26,680
Mr. Joestar,

171
00:17:27,040 --> 00:17:29,477
doesn't it seem strange
that our enemy waited

172
00:17:29,560 --> 00:17:32,442
until Polnareff was alone
before showing himself?

173
00:17:32,600 --> 00:17:33,740
I cannot help it.

174
00:17:33,880 --> 00:17:38,720
My instincts keep telling me that this
was just a ploy to lure him away from us.

175
00:17:41,740 --> 00:17:44,937
Frankly, I feel exactly
the same way myself, Avdol.

176
00:17:45,020 --> 00:17:51,480
And we can't just leave things like this
when our comrade might be in danger!

177
00:17:52,260 --> 00:17:54,460
And so, let's get in the truck now.

178
00:17:55,040 --> 00:17:56,260
And find him?

179
00:18:05,200 --> 00:18:06,030
What's that?

180
00:18:06,200 --> 00:18:07,660
You say you've seen him?

181
00:18:08,180 --> 00:18:09,220
Uh, yes.

182
00:18:10,420 --> 00:18:11,940
You're sure you saw him?

183
00:18:12,120 --> 00:18:15,460
A man whose hands are
both right hands. Well?

184
00:18:18,720 --> 00:18:20,280
Now, where is he?

185
00:18:21,760 --> 00:18:23,800
On the street, over there.

186
00:18:29,640 --> 00:18:32,460
So he is here, at last.

187
00:18:41,360 --> 00:18:42,280
Oh, shit.

188
00:18:42,640 --> 00:18:44,522
This traffic is backed up solid.

189
00:18:49,100 --> 00:18:52,453
We're not going to make any
progress at all at this rate.

190
00:18:53,120 --> 00:18:57,238
He couldn't have gotten too far, so
let's split up and search for him.

191
00:18:58,960 --> 00:19:00,489
We'll take this direction.

192
00:19:01,480 --> 00:19:04,040
Kakyoin, stay with the truck. All right.

193
00:19:26,600 --> 00:19:28,220
This guy.

194
00:19:39,300 --> 00:19:41,960
The gun is mightier than the sword.

195
00:19:43,880 --> 00:19:46,680
Now that's a fine saying, ain't it?

196
00:19:47,780 --> 00:19:50,260
No, it's not him.

197
00:19:52,260 --> 00:19:55,560
Hey, just who the hell are you, huh?

198
00:19:57,860 --> 00:20:02,700
Name's Hull Horse, and I control the
stand that's known as the Emperor.

199
00:20:03,240 --> 00:20:05,977
I don't give a damn
about you or your stand.

200
00:20:06,060 --> 00:20:09,400
I'm looking for a man whose
hands are both right hands.

201
00:20:10,120 --> 00:20:11,917
Huh, what a rude fella.

202
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:14,000
You asked, so I introduced myself.

203
00:20:14,360 --> 00:20:15,360
Hell, never mind.

204
00:20:15,640 --> 00:20:19,228
If you're looking for my partner,
he's around here somewhere.

205
00:20:19,400 --> 00:20:20,230
What?

206
00:20:23,140 --> 00:20:23,970
Where?

207
00:20:24,053 --> 00:20:24,883
Where is he?

208
00:20:29,420 --> 00:20:33,297
Hey, I don't have a lot of time to
waste on a little shit like you.

209
00:20:33,380 --> 00:20:34,380
Where is he, huh?

210
00:20:36,060 --> 00:20:36,890
Hehehe!

211
00:20:39,460 --> 00:20:40,290
Hey, you.

212
00:20:40,373 --> 00:20:41,520
What's so funny?

213
00:20:44,560 --> 00:20:46,520
Know what Lord Dio told me?

214
00:20:46,700 --> 00:20:50,560
That guy Polnareff has a habit
of underestimating his enemies,

215
00:20:50,860 --> 00:20:52,389
so it's easy to whoop him.

216
00:20:52,700 --> 00:20:56,060
It really is true, so I just had to laugh.

217
00:20:56,840 --> 00:20:57,670
What?

218
00:20:59,580 --> 00:21:04,462
If you're saying I have to beat you to get
to him, well then you give me no choice.

219
00:21:06,060 --> 00:21:07,660
...but to grant your wish.

220
00:21:13,060 --> 00:21:13,890
It cannot be.

221
00:21:14,740 --> 00:21:17,100
Do not do anything rash, Polnareff.

222
00:21:24,060 --> 00:21:25,413
No need to rush things.

223
00:21:25,920 --> 00:21:30,520
Hey, Polnareff, you ever heard of
that game called Soldier's Chess?

224
00:21:32,300 --> 00:21:33,537
Soldier's Chess?

225
00:21:33,620 --> 00:21:37,660
The tank is stronger than the
soldier, but weaker than the mine.

226
00:21:38,440 --> 00:21:43,240
Anyway, it's a game based on the
fundamental principles of battle and such.

227
00:21:43,540 --> 00:21:46,900
In the case of Whole Horses
Emperor and you, well,

228
00:21:47,160 --> 00:21:50,620
the rules of Soldier's Tests
apply perfectly, you see.

229
00:21:52,100 --> 00:21:55,720
That is, the gun's mightier
than the sword, my friend.

230
00:21:56,140 --> 00:21:58,797
Look, just what the hell are
you trying to get at anyway?

231
00:21:58,880 --> 00:22:04,000
You see, my stand is the gun,
so your sword can't beat my gun.

232
00:22:04,460 --> 00:22:05,320
What's that?

233
00:22:05,600 --> 00:22:07,200
I can beat your bum?

234
00:22:07,440 --> 00:22:09,160
Oh, you're into that stuff!

235
00:22:32,300 --> 00:22:33,137
You...

236
00:22:33,220 --> 00:22:35,180
I'll fucking kill you!

237
00:22:44,720 --> 00:22:48,580
You underestimated me,
Polnareff. You lose.

238
00:22:56,940 --> 00:23:00,340
You think I can't strike
down a bullet like that?

239
00:23:00,680 --> 00:23:01,840
Piece of cake!

240
00:23:04,500 --> 00:23:05,680
Silver, cheerio!

241
00:23:12,620 --> 00:23:13,450
What?

242
00:23:13,660 --> 00:23:14,680
It can't be!

243
00:23:15,020 --> 00:23:16,217
It changed directions!

244
00:23:16,300 --> 00:23:18,840
Even the bullet is part of my stand.

245
00:23:19,300 --> 00:23:20,300
Now I gotcha.

246
00:23:20,600 --> 00:23:22,277
You didn't expect that, did ya?

247
00:23:22,360 --> 00:23:24,040
Now you're gonna die!

248
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:40,320
What the...

249
00:23:44,420 --> 00:23:45,250
Abdul!

250
00:23:45,333 --> 00:23:47,820
I was worried, so I came looking for you.

251
00:23:48,140 --> 00:23:49,620
You worried about me?

252
00:23:49,900 --> 00:23:52,777
The enemy knows everything
there is to know about us.

253
00:23:52,860 --> 00:23:55,272
You said you had battled alone until now.

254
00:23:55,480 --> 00:23:57,715
But from now on, you cannot win alone.

255
00:23:58,520 --> 00:23:59,380
Why, you?

256
00:23:59,640 --> 00:24:01,380
Are you still lecturing me?

257
00:24:01,840 --> 00:24:02,940
Well, well.

258
00:24:04,340 --> 00:24:07,811
You picked a hell of a time to
interfere with our showdown.

259
00:24:08,340 --> 00:24:09,170
See?

260
00:24:10,100 --> 00:24:11,629
Out of the way, Polnareff.

261
00:24:11,800 --> 00:24:13,447
The bullet, it is returning.

262
00:24:13,940 --> 00:24:16,646
He is able to control
the path of this bullet.

263
00:24:19,380 --> 00:24:22,140
You can avoid a sword,
but what about this?

264
00:24:22,360 --> 00:24:24,300
I'll burn it away. Magicians!

265
00:24:33,120 --> 00:24:33,950
Abdo-san!

266
00:24:54,240 --> 00:24:55,640
Hey, the bullet!

267
00:24:55,940 --> 00:24:56,900
Andrew-san!

268
00:25:21,160 --> 00:25:22,260
Old man!

269
00:25:22,900 --> 00:25:24,760
What's the matter, Shotaro?

270
00:25:26,980 --> 00:25:29,480
I have a bad feeling about this.

271
00:25:49,500 --> 00:25:51,580
Whoa, now this is fortunate.

272
00:25:52,060 --> 00:25:53,700
You see, my gun and J.

273
00:25:53,820 --> 00:25:57,360
Giles' mirror, they just don't
get along with Abdel's fire.

274
00:25:57,600 --> 00:25:59,012
Yes, they're very lucky.

275
00:25:59,360 --> 00:26:03,537
For us, there are no more pieces to
worry about in this soldier's chest.

276
00:26:05,780 --> 00:26:07,860
Oh, Abdel, sir.

277
00:26:11,060 --> 00:26:12,340
It can't be.

278
00:26:19,860 --> 00:26:21,337
Wake up, Avdol-san.

279
00:26:21,420 --> 00:26:23,120
Open your eyes, please.

280
00:26:27,120 --> 00:26:28,340
How pathetic.

281
00:26:28,800 --> 00:26:32,506
You like to lecture others so
much and just look what happened.

282
00:26:36,740 --> 00:26:39,380
What did you say, Polnareff?

283
00:26:39,820 --> 00:26:41,740
Because he tried to save you.

284
00:26:42,040 --> 00:26:43,080
Avdol-san is...

285
00:26:44,960 --> 00:26:46,900
Who asked him to save me?

286
00:26:47,300 --> 00:26:50,440
What a nosy meddler, always lecturing me.

287
00:26:50,740 --> 00:26:53,060
A guy like him gets to be a drag.

288
00:26:53,760 --> 00:26:56,878
That's why I told you that
I wanted to do this alone.

289
00:26:58,320 --> 00:27:02,060
Polnareff, I can't believe I'm
hearing this from you right now.

290
00:27:12,500 --> 00:27:14,400
It's so damned annoying.

291
00:27:18,580 --> 00:27:24,020
For someone to die right before my eyes
like that, that is so goddamned annoying!

292
00:28:40,220 --> 00:28:41,050
Thank you.

293
00:29:05,440 --> 00:29:08,240
Let's go.

294
00:29:35,800 --> 00:29:37,480
Thank you.

295
00:30:04,860 --> 00:30:07,660
Thank you.
